<span id="variable:CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET_NAME"></span><h1>CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET_NAME<a class="headerlink" href="#cmake-global-autorcc-target-name" title="Link to this heading">¶</a></h1>
<div class="versionadded">
<p><span class="versionmodified added">New in version 3.14.</span></p>
</div>
<p>Change the name of the global <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">autorcc</span></code> target.</p>
<p>When <span class="target" id="index-0-variable:CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET"></span><a class="reference internal" href="CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET.html#variable:CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET" title="CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET"><code class="xref cmake cmake-variable docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET</span></code></a> is enabled, a global custom target
named <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">autorcc</span></code> is created.  <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET_NAME</span></code>
allows to set a different name for that target.</p>
<p>By default <code class="docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CMAKE_GLOBAL_AUTORCC_TARGET_NAME</span></code> is unset.</p>
<p>See the <span class="target" id="index-0-manual:cmake-qt(7)"></span><a class="reference internal" href="../manual/cmake-qt.7.html#manual:cmake-qt(7)" title="cmake-qt(7)"><code class="xref cmake cmake-manual docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">cmake-qt(7)</span></code></a> manual for more information on using CMake
with Qt.</p>
</section>


