<span id="variable:CMAKE_EXECUTABLE_ENABLE_EXPORTS"></span><h1>CMAKE_EXECUTABLE_ENABLE_EXPORTS<a class="headerlink" href="#cmake-executable-enable-exports" title="Link to this heading">¶</a></h1>
<div class="versionadded">
<p><span class="versionmodified added">New in version 3.27.</span></p>
</div>
<p>Specify whether executables export symbols for loadable modules.</p>
<p>This variable is used to initialize the <span class="target" id="index-0-prop_tgt:ENABLE_EXPORTS"></span><a class="reference internal" href="../prop_tgt/ENABLE_EXPORTS.html#prop_tgt:ENABLE_EXPORTS" title="ENABLE_EXPORTS"><code class="xref cmake cmake-prop_tgt docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">ENABLE_EXPORTS</span></code></a> target
property for executable targets when they are created by calls to the
<span class="target" id="index-0-command:add_executable"></span><a class="reference internal" href="../command/add_executable.html#command:add_executable" title="add_executable"><code class="xref cmake cmake-command docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">add_executable()</span></code></a> command.  See the property documentation for details.</p>
<p>This variable supersede the <span class="target" id="index-0-variable:CMAKE_ENABLE_EXPORTS"></span><a class="reference internal" href="CMAKE_ENABLE_EXPORTS.html#variable:CMAKE_ENABLE_EXPORTS" title="CMAKE_ENABLE_EXPORTS"><code class="xref cmake cmake-variable docutils literal notranslate"><span class="pre">CMAKE_ENABLE_EXPORTS</span></code></a> variable.</p>
