<span id="amdgpu-synid-gfx1030-vaddr-a5639c"></span><h1>vaddr<a class="headerlink" href="#vaddr" title="Link to this heading">¶</a></h1>
<p>Image address which includes from one to four dimensional coordinates and other data used to locate a position in the image.</p>
<p>This operand may be specified using either <a class="reference internal" href="../AMDGPUOperandSyntax.html#amdgpu-synid-v"><span class="std std-ref">standard VGPR syntax</span></a> or special <a class="reference internal" href="../AMDGPUOperandSyntax.html#amdgpu-synid-nsa"><span class="std std-ref">NSA VGPR syntax</span></a>.</p>
<p><em>Size:</em> 1-12 dwords. Actual size depends on opcode, <a class="reference internal" href="../AMDGPUModifierSyntax.html#amdgpu-synid-dim"><span class="std std-ref">dim</span></a> and <a class="reference internal" href="../AMDGPUModifierSyntax.html#amdgpu-synid-a16"><span class="std std-ref">a16</span></a>.</p>
<p><em>Operands:</em> <a class="reference internal" href="../AMDGPUOperandSyntax.html#amdgpu-synid-v"><span class="std std-ref">v</span></a></p>
